{"id": "EUVD-2026-93316", "enisaUuid": "aa3a0ac1-f928-325a-916f-1460c6239543", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: unlist vifs when their netdev is unregistered\n\nmac80211 only removes vifs from the local->interfaces list when\nan interface is removed via ieee80211_if_remove(), before it\nunregisters the netdev. However, it's possible for a netdev to\nbe unregistered without going through that: When the netns that\nholds the wiphy is destroyed, the wiphy is supposed to move to\nthe init_ns, but that can run into allocation failures.\n\nThen, mac80211 has an interface listed that doesn't exist, and\nwill eventually hit\n\n  BUG: failure at net/wireless/core.h:141/wiphy_to_rdev()!\n  ...\n  _cfg80211_unregister_wdev+0x24/0x36a [cfg80211]\n  cfg80211_unregister_wdev+0x15/0x1d [cfg80211]\n  ieee80211_remove_interfaces+0x1ff/0x257 [mac80211]\n  ieee80211_unregister_hw+0x73/0x1d1 [mac80211]\n  mac80211_hwsim_del_radio+0x114/0x166 [mac80211_hwsim]\n\nRemove the interface from the list in ->ndo_uninit if it's still\naround to avoid this.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:41", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a22c02863439993095acd0c3db97fa53cd515f4f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/20a56e96a6f7b4dfbd13f8732fd2673409fc7ba0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b735ad1a9aca6080192c1316cf2706e5e1318762", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d45bf731ec7085d2cc2c5d179d3b3b6c743d4fb1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/821bab0456dfca12acef6df702c8f2477d313227", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eee2efd82867b623982ac51925b5a1812a74c50d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wm55-5w39-6wj2", "CVE-2026-98331"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "028bb8a9-9a2a-3ebb-85e5-c42602672f57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "463d018323851a608eef52a9427b0585005c647f <a22c02863439993095acd0c3db97fa53cd515f4f"}, {"id": "31e7fe09-9c19-30df-9fe1-0b6489abe160", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "3f785d49-e8cc-3d75-843d-d2474403b446", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "463d018323851a608eef52a9427b0585005c647f <b735ad1a9aca6080192c1316cf2706e5e1318762"}, {"id": "5327269a-3315-32e5-be3a-e88e4ebca755", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "463d018323851a608eef52a9427b0585005c647f <20a56e96a6f7b4dfbd13f8732fd2673409fc7ba0"}, {"id": "672e65c2-ff0e-3b06-a5d5-761653d463bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "6b1def72-c6e2-3672-959f-28c9ff787adb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "6bf142cf-9e0f-30f8-8aee-840d1e575628", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.32"}, {"id": "74374311-7d3b-323f-8bb4-486a121a6b2e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "463d018323851a608eef52a9427b0585005c647f <d45bf731ec7085d2cc2c5d179d3b3b6c743d4fb1"}, {"id": "9193ff9f-0294-309d-9945-965a46a4d62c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "960c795b-3b06-3c95-a966-063a100c1395", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "463d018323851a608eef52a9427b0585005c647f <eee2efd82867b623982ac51925b5a1812a74c50d"}, {"id": "a02ee3b3-7d70-322a-a6cc-f05b6d496cfd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "463d018323851a608eef52a9427b0585005c647f <821bab0456dfca12acef6df702c8f2477d313227"}, {"id": "a8544fff-a902-3308-b672-76b5beb6fee5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1